Tulipora - Privacy Policy

Last updated: 26 November 2026

Tulipora is a mobile logic puzzle game made by CodingTech Studio, Başakşehir / İstanbul, Türkiye ("we").
Contact: codingtechstudio@gmail.com

Tulipora is made for adults. It is not directed to children and we do not knowingly collect data from children.


1. What stays on your device

Your progress, coins, hints, collection, achievements, daily puzzle streak and settings are stored only on your device. We have no account system and no server of our own. Deleting the game deletes this data. What the game sends for statistics and crash reports is described in section 2.


2. Play statistics and crash reports

The game uses Google Firebase:
- Crash reports (Firebase Crashlytics): if the game crashes, a report with the error, the device model, the operating system and app version and a random installation identifier is sent, so that we can fix the error. This is our legitimate interest in a working game; the report contains nothing you typed and no account.
- Play statistics (Firebase Analytics): only if you allow them in the "Play statistics" window or in Settings > Play statistics. Then the game sends events such as a puzzle started or finished, its rule and difficulty, hints and rewards used, together with a random app-instance identifier and general device information (model, operating system, language, country). They are used only to improve the game, never for ads, and you can switch them off at any time. Without your permission nothing is collected.


3. Ads

The game shows ads through Google AdMob: videos you choose to watch for a reward (a hint, a continue, double coins or keeping your daily streak), full-screen ads between some puzzles, and a banner at the bottom of the puzzle screen. To show and measure ads, Google receives the advertising identifier of your device, your IP address (from which an approximate location is derived), device information and your interactions with the ads.

In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, a consent form from Google asks for your choice before any ad is requested. Elsewhere the game asks with its own window ("Allow" / "Don't allow"). Without your consent to personalised ads, only non-personalised ads are requested. You can reopen your choice at any time under Settings > Privacy > Options. You can also reset or delete the advertising identifier in your device settings.

"Remove ads" in the shop turns off the ads between puzzles and the banner; videos for rewards stay available if you want them.

How Google uses data from apps that use its services: https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites


4. Purchases

If you buy something in the shop, the payment is handled entirely by Google Play (or the App Store). We never see your card or payment details. The game only learns from the store which product was bought and keeps the transaction identifier on your device so that a product is delivered once. "Restore purchases" in the shop asks the store again which one-time products your store account owns.


5. Who receives data

Google Ireland Limited / Google LLC, as the provider of Firebase, AdMob and Google Play billing. Google may process data on servers outside your country, including the United States; it relies on the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses. We do not sell your data and we share it with no one else.

Rating window and our other games: the game may ask Google Play to show its own rating window, and Settings lists our other games with a link to their Google Play pages. Tapping a link opens Google Play. We send no data for either; the link only tells Google Play which of our games it was opened from. What you do in Google Play is covered by Google's privacy policy.


6. How long data is kept

Data on your device: until you delete the game or its data. Play statistics: at most 14 months. Crash reports: 90 days. Ad data is kept by Google under its own policies.


7. Your rights

Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR, the UK GDPR or the Turkish Law No. 6698, KVKK), you have the right to ask what data is held about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to object to or restrict its use, to withdraw your consent at any time, and to complain to your data protection authority. We hold no account or name on our side: play statistics and crash reports are tied only to random identifiers that we cannot link to you. You can switch play statistics off in Settings, change your ad choice in the game and reset your advertising identifier, and you can write to codingtechstudio@gmail.com with any question. We answer within 30 days.


8. Permissions

Internet access and network state (ads, purchases, crash reports and play statistics), the advertising identifier (ads), billing (purchases through Google Play), vibration (short feedback pulses you can switch off in Settings), and wake lock, foreground service and install referrer, which the Google libraries use to send their data reliably.


9. Changes

If this policy changes, the date at the top changes and the new text is published at the same address.


